# FR-250: runs emitrust-bx's pytest suite inside the fast lit tier. It pins
# the bijection laws as PROPERTIES (>= 500 generated Kernel functions, law 1
# and law 2 on the Rust side in pure python and on the C++ side through real
# clang), plus per-module unit tests. Bytecode/cache writes are disabled so a
# test run never dirties the source tree.
# The suite is split into 4 shards (pytest-0..3.test, --bx-shard=K/4 in
# tests/conftest.py) so no single lit test nears the 600s per-test cap; the
# shards partition the suite by collection index mod 4.
# RUN: env PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 %python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider %bx_src/tests --bx-shard=1/4
